.TH GENESIS-MEMORY 7 "October 2026" "Genesis 0.2.0" "Genesis Manual"
.SH NAME
genesis-memory \- the memory architecture of the Genesis mind
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBtemporal_lobe.concepts\fR        the concept network and its canonical edge log
\fBtemporal_lobe.concepts.holographic\fR  fixed-size associative store (HRR)
\fBtemporal_lobe.concepts.archive\fR      cold-storage tier
\fBInner_World.memory\fR            working, semantic, procedural, and
                                  biologically-grounded subsystems
\fBltm_store.* / stm_ring.bin\fR    the body's persistence (daemon-owned)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Genesis has several memories, not one \(em and the honest description
of where a fact lives is "which tier, written by which process." The
daemon owns the body's persistence; the mind's working, semantic, and
procedural layers sit on top.
.SS The concept network and the edge log
The concept network
.RI ( temporal_lobe/concepts )
is the symbolic knowledge graph at the core of cognition. Its edge
list is not an independently persisted structure \(em it is a fold
over
.IR edge_log.jsonl ,
the canonical, append-only log. Two record kinds matter:
.IP \(bu 2
.B assert
\(em upsert an edge, carrying absolute weight; re-assertion is
reinforcement.
.IP \(bu 2
.B retract
\(em tombstone an edge; the fold drops it.
.PP
A
.B snapshot
line replaces the fold base \(em used by sleep compression and by
seeding an empty log; compaction rewrites the file as one snapshot of
the live fold. Edges whose content is a function of embedding
geometry \(em machine-built associations like hub attachment,
semantic bridges, co-occurrence \(em are never logged; they are
derivable, so they live in the holographic store instead.
.SS The holographic associative store
Most fuzzy similarity never becomes a graph edge at all.
.IR holographic_graph.npz
is a fixed-size holographic reduced representation (HRR / vector
symbolic architecture): associations are stored implicitly in
high-dimensional vectors by circular-convolution binding, recovered
by unbinding, and queried by resonance. It replaced the monotonically
growing auto-generated bridge edges, which dominated serialized state
and regenerated every sleep cycle. The concept network can query it
for associations beyond exact edges.
.SS Tiers
Working memory is capped; the disk is not. Concepts that fade from
working memory spill into the
.B archive
\(em a cold-storage tier preserving typed associations with their own
scope \(em and are recalled by SimHash similarity when the active set
has no answer (\fBFIND_SIMILAR_ARCHIVED\fR, \fBUNARCHIVE_EPISODE\fR,
\fBSEARCH_ARCHIVED\fR on the daemon wire).
.SS The body's persistence
The daemon owns the durable stores in the data dir:
.TP
.I ltm_store.dat " / " ltm_store.meta
Long-term episodic memory \(em append-only record bodies with a
metadata index.
.TP
.I ltm_store.traces " / " ltm_store.bundles
The SDR trace and bundle overlays layered on the same store.
.TP
.I stm_ring.bin
The short-term ring buffer \(em recent experience before
consolidation.
.TP
.I edge_log.jsonl
The canonical relationship log described above.
.TP
.I holographic_graph.npz
The serialized associative store.
.PP
Two utility binaries,
.BR genesis-merge-ltm " and " genesis-merge-stm ,
fold one incarnation's stores into another \(em they exist so a mind
rescued off a dead machine can rejoin a living one, memory intact.
.SS The cognitive subsystems
.IR Inner_World/memory
holds the biologically-grounded layers the graph alone does not
cover: working memory (the active context scratchpad that lets a
conversation be a conversation), semantic and procedural memory,
spaced repetition, emotional memory and priming, attractor-style
pattern completion over the SimHash store, and forgetting \(em
decay is a mechanism, not a leak.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $DATA_DIR/edge_log.jsonl
Canonical edge log \(em the single source of truth for relationships.
.TP
.I $DATA_DIR/ltm_store.* , $DATA_DIR/stm_ring.bin , $DATA_DIR/holographic_graph.npz
The body's persistence.
